<h1><a name=3D"_Toc519676243"></a><a name=3Dintroducction><span style=3D'ms=
o-bookmark:
_Toc519676243'>INTRODUCCTION</span></a></h1>

<div class=3DMsoNormal align=3Dcenter style=3D'text-align:center'>

<hr size=3D3 width=3D"100%" align=3Dcenter>

</div>

<p class=3DFirstParagraph>This is a simulation of the Humboldt Squid popula=
tion
off Chilean waters. The time scale is month. The recruitments are modelled
using Beverton and Holt stock-recruitment relationship (Beverton and Holt 1=
957)
with a steepness parameter (h) (Mace and Doonan 1988) and process errors
(rsigma). Recruitment can also be multiply by a seasonal factor to generate=
 a
seasonal pattern. Seasonal pattern can be constant (no effect), exponential
decreasing or sinusoidal.</p>

<p class=3DMsoBodyText>This simulator is coded in R Mardown in R Studio (Al=
laire
et al. 2018). The individual and population parameters are setting in a file
named “HSquid_Par.csv”. The use of external parameter file allows to run the
simulation with different set of parameters.</p>

<p class=3DMsoBodyText>So far no fishing is included in the simulation.</p>

<h1><a name=3D"_Toc519676244"></a><a name=3Dmethods><span style=3D'mso-book=
mark:_Toc519676244'>METHODS</span></a></h1>

<div class=3DMsoNormal align=3Dcenter style=3D'text-align:center'>

<hr size=3D3 width=3D"100%" align=3Dcenter>

</div>

